In what follows, when we write that a variable is regressed on a spline basis, we mean that OLS is used for the regression. In Theorems 6 and 7 below, we use the terminology that $T$ is computed using spline regressions if the regressions (following the notation of Algorithm 1) are as follows:
• $\hat v\equiv1$ for simplicity;
• $\hat g$ is formed by regressing $Y$ onto $\phi(X,Z)$;
• $\tilde m$ is formed by regressing $\hat g(X,Z)$ onto $\phi^Z(Z)$, or equivalently by regressing $Y$ onto $\phi^Z(Z)$;
• $\hat m_{\hat f}$ and $\hat m$ are formed by regressing $\hat f(X,Z)$ and $Y$, respectively, on $\psi(Z)$.
In addition, we also omit discussion of the sign correction step (Algorithm 1, Step 1(iv)), since $\hat\rho$ is always non-negative for the estimators given above.
